      "notes": "Backrooms: Overstay is an atmospheric co-op survival-horror game. Expect sustained tension,\r\ndread, and occasional jump scares, plus a psychological-horror layer. As your character's\r\nstress rises, the game produces unsettling hallucinations: distorted sounds, whispers, and a\r\nwarping, unreliable screen.\r\n\r\nViolence is mild and defensive. You use a pistol and improvised explosives to fend off\r\nfictional monstrous creatures. There is no blood, gore, or corpses. Defeated enemies simply\r\ncollapse and fade, and being defeated yourself is shown as an on-screen \"downed / bleeding\r\nout\" prompt. Themes of fear, isolation, and death run throughout, and an optional permadeath\r\nmode can end a run permanently.\r\n\r\nSurvival items include fictional first-aid supplies, a calming sedative pill, and a stimulant\r\nenergy drink, all used only as ordinary survival tools.\r\n\r\nThe game contains no sexual content or nudity, no sexual violence, no self-harm or suicide, no\r\ndrug or alcohol abuse, and no real-world hateful or extremist content. Online sessions use live\r\nproximity voice chat, so you may hear unmoderated audio from other players."
